<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Haro</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Haro was a Castilian noble family that ruled the Lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biscay">Biscay</a> from the 11th to the 14th century. Descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inigo-lopez-ezquerra">Íñigo López Ezquerra</a> and named after the town of Haro in La Rioja, its members, many called López de Haro, were among the most powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>; Diego López V founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilbao">Bilbao</a> in 1300. The lordship passed to the crown in 1379.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-haro.jpg" alt="House of Haro" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heralder · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_House_of_Haro,_Lords_of_Biscay.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
